{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "Shared red packet presentation rules for the four kits (docs/design/red-packet-v5-roles-and-wallet.md). `amountInput` / `countInput` are the composer's format-only filters (range checks stay with the host). `cardState` maps the plugin's public layer (status) and the viewer's personal layer (claimedByMe, tapAction) to the card state; `card` is the status line precedence and tap rule of RedPacketCard; `status` names the copy, which each kit resolves from its own strings: busy, statusLabel (the host text as given), tapToOpen, view, claimed, finished, expired, refunded, unavailable. The card never shows an amount, not even the viewer's own. `cardBadge` is the kind badge and the exclusive recipient line. `openSheet` is which keys the open sheet offers per state. `amount` is the integer-only amount text from a minor-unit string and the ISO 4217 exponent the contract gives (currencyExponent), plus the currency symbol table. `detail` is what RedPacketDetail draws for each viewerRole and status, from the fields the server returned (an absent amount is never drawn). `faded` is how a claimed / finished / expired / refunded card fades: each colour of the card mixed in sRGB with `targetToken` (white in light mode, a deep red in dark mode), the target taking `mixToken` (lerp(colour, target, mix)); the text on it is `inkToken`, which must keep `minTextContrast` on every faded stop the text sits on. Top-level `target` / `ink` / `stops` are light mode; `dark` holds the dark-mode values. Busy and disabled cards are never faded: they keep the unopened face and white text and change only the status line. `composer` is which amount label and rows the composer shows for the kinds a host offers: amountLabel names the copy (total, each, amount).",
